The value that is to be put in at every one of the places is that which the power of a hundred gives when it is divided by the whole number. In that way the ratio that enters into the two figures is made everywhere the same, and the figures themselves fall to the one and only common value. They are afterwards to be set down in order that they may be seen, and the array is to be put into the place where it is to be looked for.

